      "category": "bug",
      "title": "Restyle check may force perpetual updates",
      "message": "The check compares the stored row background against the focused or unfocused selection color without considering whether the row is actually selected. Rows in SelectedIDs that are disabled or restyled differently may always mismatch, forcing Update() on every sync. Also, the comparison happens on every syncChoice, and bg.At(0,0) on non-uniform images may panic or give wrong results. The Convert type assertion is safe for NRGBAModel, but a nil Styles.Background is treated as stale and triggers constant updates.",
      "suggestion": "Skip rows that have not been styled yet and only trigger an update when a styled selected row is stale. Guard against non-uniform backgrounds.",
